# SUPPQUAL study data for the strict `SUPP--` token (Fix #160).
#
# These are the CONTROL half of the AP/SQ fixture set: SUPP datasets already exist in
# /data/testdata (24 of them, including the split forms supplbch/supplbhe/supplbur), so a
# behaviour that holds here and not for AP/SQ is a family-specific defect rather than a
# broken fixture.
#
# ⚠ A SUPPQUAL dataset carries RDOMAIN and NOT a DOMAIN column. That is what makes
# OperationExecutor.unsplitNameFromData take its second branch ("SUPP" + RDOMAIN) instead of
# reading a DOMAIN cell — so the column set here is load-bearing, not decoration. Column names
# and order follow SDTMIG v3.4 §8.4 and the shipped /data/testdata/test_20/SUPPLB.json.

dataset SUPPLB label="Supplemental Qualifiers for LB"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
col QORIG    type=Char label="Origin"
col QEVAL    type=Char label="Evaluator"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | LBSEQ | 1 | LBTMSHI | Lab Result/Upper Limit of Normal | 0.8 | DERIVED | CLINICAL STUDY SPONSOR
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1023 | LBSEQ | 2 | LBTMSHI | Lab Result/Upper Limit of Normal | 1.1 | DERIVED | CLINICAL STUDY SPONSOR
---

# The javadoc's headline split case: an 8-character NAME whose data-derived base is the
# 6-character SUPPLB, which strict `SUPP--` matches. The name-only heuristic strips one letter
# and yields SUPPLBH (7), which `SUPP--` misses — so this dataset is what separates the
# production data path from the table-less fallback.
dataset SUPPLBHM label="Supplemental Qualifiers for LB (Hematology)"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
col QORIG    type=Char label="Origin"
col QEVAL    type=Char label="Evaluator"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | LBSEQ | 3 | LBFAST | Fasting Status | Y | CRF | INVESTIGATOR
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1023 | LBSEQ | 4 | LBFAST | Fasting Status | N | CRF | INVESTIGATOR
---

# ⚠ The ONE shape strict `SUPP--` deliberately cannot express: RDOMAIN=APFA gives the
# 8-character base SUPPAPFA, and the name itself is 10 characters, so neither the name leg
# (SUPP + exactly 2) nor the split-base leg reaches it. SDTMIG v3.4 §8.4.2 requires exactly
# this dataset to be renamed SQAPFAMH (see sq-family.cdt), which is why the inexpressibility of
# `SUPP--` here is by design and must NOT be "fixed" by reintroducing the deleted SUPP/AP
# family wildcard.
#
# ⚑ RESOLVED 2026-08-07 (decision W4; authored by wave-13 lane A, edit set E). The shape is
# expressible without any matcher change: `SUPPAPFA--` is prefix.length()+2 = 10 and matches
# this dataset on the NAME leg. `firstMatchingDomainEntry` computes that for ANY prefix — there
# is no closed list — so this was a MISSING TOKEN, never a missing mechanism. The four rules
# whose Check is `dataset_name longer_than 8` (CDISC-CG0018, CORE-000357, CDISC-CG0205,
# CORE-000293) now carry `SUPPAPFA--`, which restores the canonical target their own cited
# guidance names and which Fix #170 had unmasked as unreachable. ⚠ Note this is NOT the family
# wildcard returning: `SUPPAPFA--` matches ONLY 10-character names beginning SUPPAPFA.
dataset SUPPAPFAMH label="Supplemental Qualifiers for APFA (Medical History)"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
col QORIG    type=Char label="Origin"
col QEVAL    type=Char label="Evaluator"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | APFA | 01-701-1015 | FASEQ | 1 | FAEVLINT | Evaluation Interval | -P1D | DERIVED | CLINICAL STUDY SPONSOR
---
